    {
      "_comment": "THE DISCRIMINATOR. RFC-MACP-0012 Section 4.1, Denominator: for supermajority the denominator is the decisive votes (approve or reject), and abstentions are excluded. The ratio is 1 APPROVE / 1 decisive = 1.0 >= 0.67, so the result is Passed. A runtime that counts the ABSTAIN in the denominator computes 1/2 = 0.5 < 0.67 and denies this message, and one that divides by the declared participants computes 1/3. A runtime that treats the BLOCK evaluation as a veto also denies it.",
